@ifnottex
@node Top
@top ETL Madness FlowUI

This manual documents @strong{FlowUI} (Flow Builder Studio), the interactive
.NET 10 ASP.NET Core Blazor Server web application for visually designing,
configuring, signing, encrypting, validating, executing, and monitoring XML
ETL pipelines powered by @code{go-flow} and @code{go-flowAPI}.

@menu
* Overview and Architecture::   Stateless frontend design and package layout.
* Invoking flow-ui::            Command-line options and launcher wrapper.
* Configuration File::          Syntax and variables for @file{flow-ui.env}.
* OS Services and Daemons::     systemd, OpenRC, SysVinit, FreeBSD/OpenBSD rc.d, launchd, and Windows SCM.
@end menu
@end ifnottex

@node Overview and Architecture
@chapter Overview and Architecture

@code{FlowUI} is a stateless visual studio and orchestration frontend built on
.NET 10 ASP.NET Core Blazor Server. It does not connect directly to any
application database; all artifact persistence, validation, execution, SSE
streaming, user/group/pipeline-group/ACL administration, and telemetry flow
over HTTP/HTTPS to @code{go-flowAPI}.

Packages install isolated under @file{/opt/flow-ui} on Unix platforms
(Linux, macOS, FreeBSD, and OpenBSD) and
@file{C:\Program Files\ETL Madness\Flow UI\} on Windows, so FlowUI can be
installed side-by-side with @code{go-flow} (@file{/opt/flow}) and
@code{go-flowAPI} (@file{/opt/flow-api}) with zero file collisions.

@node Invoking flow-ui
@chapter Invoking @code{flow-ui}

Synopsis:

@example
flow-ui [--env-file PATH] [--urls URLS] [--contentRoot PATH] [--service-name NAME]
flow-ui --version | --help
@end example

On Unix systems, @file{/opt/flow-ui/bin/flow-ui} launches the published .NET 10
application in @file{/opt/flow-ui/app/} with @option{--contentRoot /opt/flow-ui/app}
so static assets and embedded documentation resolve regardless of the caller's
working directory.

@node Configuration File
@chapter Configuration File (@file{flow-ui.env})

@code{flow-ui.env} uses @code{KEY=VALUE} syntax. Existing non-empty process
environment variables take precedence over values in the file.

@itemize @bullet
@item @code{ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT}: Recommended value @code{Production}.
@item @code{ASPNETCORE_URLS}: Explicit Kestrel listen URLs (e.g., @code{http://0.0.0.0:5185}).
@item @code{FLOW_API_URL}: Base URL of @code{go-flowAPI} (e.g., @code{http://localhost:8080}).
@item @code{FLOW_UI_AUTH_MODE}: @code{ApiBasic} (default) or @code{Windows}.
@item @code{FLOW_API_BASIC_AUTH}: Optional Base64 service token for @code{Windows} mode.
@end itemize

@node OS Services and Daemons
@chapter OS Services and Daemons

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Linux systemd}: @file{/usr/lib/systemd/system/flow-ui.service} (user @code{flowui}, state @file{/var/lib/flow-ui}).
@item @strong{Linux OpenRC / SysVinit}: Templates in @file{/opt/flow-ui/share/services/}.
@item @strong{FreeBSD rc.d}: @file{/usr/local/etc/rc.d/flow_ui} (enable via @code{sysrc flow_ui_enable="YES"}; requires FreeBSD @code{dotnet} package).
@item @strong{OpenBSD rc.d}: @file{/etc/rc.d/flow_ui} (enable via @code{rcctl enable flow_ui}; requires a custom/ported .NET 10 runtime on OpenBSD).
@item @strong{macOS launchd}: @file{/opt/flow-ui/share/services/launchd/com.etlmadness.flow-ui.plist}.
@item @strong{Windows SCM}: Native Windows Service support in @file{FlowUI.exe} with @file{Install-FlowUIService.ps1} and @file{Uninstall-FlowUIService.ps1}.
@end itemize

